{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith","id":1287057,"title":"Barthes is wrong; Allen, Cosby, and Smith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-12T08:18:03-08:00","id":1287057,"title":"Barthes is wrong; Allen, Cosby, and Smith","content":"&quot;The Death of the Author&quot; is a 1967 essay by the French literary critic and theorist Roland Barthes (1915\u201380). Barthes' essay argues against traditional literary criticism's practice of incorporating the intentions and biographical context of an author in an interpretation of a text, and instead argues that writing and creator are unrelated.<br /> <br /> Barthes is wrong.<br /> <br /> Zak \u201cSabbath\u201d Smith is a grotesque person and a good game designer. Some of that matters, and some does not. The same is true of people like Woody Allen, Bill Cosby, and others.<br /> <br /> I am not defending these men - I cannot and will not defend these men.<br /> <br /> However, <i>Vornhiem</i> is good, and so is <i>Red and Pleasant Land</i>. This observation asks the same question of Smith that people ask of Cosby and Allen. Cosby's old stand up routines, and TV shows were funny \u2013 they were mostly good at what they were supposed to do. Allen is a talented filmmaker \u2013 his movies are mostly good at what they are supposed to do.<br /> <br /> Are they worth it? Are they worth the money you have you pay to watch them, or buy the books? Please remember that some portion of that money goes to Cosby, Allen, and Smith. Are the commercial products (i.e. artifacts) these men produce worth the time required to watch or read?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Death of the Author posits the artifact is its own thing and independent of its creators or creation. This is the wrong approach. We are in a situation where the author, and authorial behavior and intent as best we can determine them, are more important than the artifact.<br /> <br /> We do not have the luxury of any other approach.<br /> <br /> It does not matter that Allen\u2019s <i>Love and Death</i> (1975) is a funny movie. It does not matter that Cosby\u2019s <i>I Started out as a Child</i> (1963) is a funny stand up performance. It does not matter that both <i>Vornhiem</i> and <i>Red and Pleasant Land</i> are good RPG products. It matters that the men behind these productions are terrible people, who do not deserve support of any kind.<br /> <br /> The same is true of most other \u201cproblematic\u201d creators and producers. And the people who support and enable the abuse these men perpetuate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T08:52:17-08:00","id":1287065,"title":"","content":"Yep. Only way that argument can hold any water is if we were somehow in a shortage of creative people who weren't abusive monsters. We aren't, so they can die miserable, alone, and hated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T08:53:11-08:00","id":1287066,"title":"","content":"&quot;All autobiography is storytelling; all writing is autobiography.&quot;- J. M. Coetzee<br /> <br /> All things considered, I'd have to agree. Creatives are their creations in a very real way, inextricably linked, regardless of medium. As a comedian, I can make jokes, often dark or controversial ones, but those, and everything I write or create, are an extension of me. I don't, and shouldn't, have the freedom to distance myself from what I make or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 02-12-2019, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T09:23:32-08:00","id":1287075,"title":"","content":"I know I'm going to get a lot of flak for this, and let it be known that this was supposed be the only post I will make on this matter. After this, I don't want to be going anywhere near this drama with a thirty-nine-and-a-half foot pole.<br /> <br /> As someone who utterly detests the deeds and character of Woody Allen, Bill Cosby, and especially Zak Smith, I'm still going to have to disagree with this thread.<br /> <br /> I am a firm believer in free speech, preservation of history, and keeping the author separate from the work, unless the work in question is directly reflective of the author's views (or is directly connected to his crimes).<br /> <br /> Examples of such works that actually are problematic and cannot be subject to &quot;Death of the Author&quot; would include Mein Kampf, The Communist Manifesto, Chick Tracts, and The 120 Days of Sodom. Those examples cannot be separated from the author, because they are intended as a reflection of the author himself. Cosby's stand-up and Zak's games are not in that category, even if Bill Cosby and Zak Smith themselves are vile evil excuses for human beings.<br /> <br /> To unperson an entire body of work because the person in question is a scumbag is pure unadulterated totalitarian mob mentality bullshit taken right out of the playbook of Joseph Stalin and Vladimir Lenin.<br /> <br /> Yes, Zak Smith is a vile excuse for a human being and should be punished for his behavior, and I will not defend him or his actions. In fact, I hated him even before these recent revelations came to light.<br /> <br /> But there are other &quot;problematic&quot; games created by certain nameless people who have engaged in utterly reprehensible behavior, some of whom used to work for this very company. I could go further into detail, but I will stop here on that specific subject for the sake of civility and respect.<br /> <br /> TL;DR I am opposed to real-life abuse, but censoring fiction like we live under totalitarian rule is not going to solve anything. If you don't like Zak Smith as a person and find his games problematic, then do what I do and simply don't buy them.<br /> <br /> Censoring his works and erasing them from history won't undo the abuses he committed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 02-13-2019, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T11:04:38-08:00","id":1287115,"title":"","content":"This isn\u2019t what death of the author means. Death of the author isn\u2019t concerned with the morality of consuming media produced by amoral authors, it\u2019s about interpreting a work independently of authorial intent. Death of the author doesn\u2019t say \u201cit\u2019s doesn\u2019t matter what horrible things Cosby did, it\u2019s ok to watch his standup anyway,\u201d what it says is, \u201cit doesn\u2019t matter what Rowling tweets, Wizards shitting themselves is not DeFacto canon just because she said it.\u201d Or, perhaps a more cogent example, \u201cIt doesn\u2019t matter that Tolkien said he detested allegory and vehemently denied that Lord of the Rings was an allegory for the world wars, that\u2019s still a valid interpretation of the text.\u201d<br /> <br /> Death of the author is a complicated subject, and I think Critical interpretation in the modern world needs to be more nuanced than Death of the Author would suggest. I agree that Lord of the Rings as allegory for the World Wars is a valid interpretation of the text, and a valuable way to look at it, but I also think that any critical interpretation of Lord of the Rings does itself a great disservice if it disregards Tolkien\u2019s distaste for allegory and his insistence that his Middle Earth stories were written only to give fictional context to his constructed languages.<br /> <br /> ...but it\u2019s not really what\u2019s being discussed here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287075#post1287075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Examples of such works that actually are problematic and cannot be subject to &quot;Death of the Author&quot; would include Mein Kampf, The Communist Manifesto, Chick Tracts, and The 120 Days of Sodom. Those examples cannot be separated from the author, because <b>they are intended as a reflection of the author himself</b>. Cosby's stand-up and Zak's games are not in that category, even if Bill Cosby and Zak Smith themselves are vile evil excuses for human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> See, the above is a great example of why this is a separate issue from death of the author. Camilla here is specifically choosing not to separate the art from the artist <i>because of</i> authorial intent, the very thing Death of the Author is specifically about disregarding. Death of the author would suggest that it doesn\u2019t matter if a work is <i>intended</i> to be reflective of the author or not, all that matters is if you interpret a reflection of the author in the work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287075#post1287075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DR I am opposed to real-life abuse, but censoring fiction like we live under totalitarian rule is not going to solve anything. If you don't like Zak Smith as a person and find his games problematic, then do what I do and simply don't buy them.<br /> <br /> Censoring his works and erasing them from history won't undo the abuses he committed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Camilla, \u201cdon\u2019t buy them\u201d is the only thing that is being advocated here. Nobody who isn\u2019t made of straw is suggesting \u201ccensoring his works and erasing them from history,\u201d so please try to relax, put down your anti-SJW pitchfork and actually engage with the discussion instead of crying \u201cLeninist\u201d every time someone suggests maybe not buying stuff written by rapists is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I have a great personal example of why \u201cseparating the art from the artist\u201d doesn\u2019t always work. My favorite musical artist from 2008 to 2018 was Will Francis, AKA William Control. He\u2019s a fucking brilliant lyricist and solid composer, and produced some of the most evocative darkwave music I have ever heard. Much of his music focuses on the theme of BDSM, which as a BDSM-practicing person, I found pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Recently, it came to light that he took advantage of his celebrity and of BDSM to rape and abuse a lot of women. Now, I already own his entire discography up to the point that this information came out, so listening to his music on my IPhone or my CD player won\u2019t make him any more money than I\u2019ve already made him. I could continue to listen to the music I\u2019ve loved for over a decade, and as long as I didn\u2019t buy anything new he released, no more of my money would make its way to him. But I can\u2019t in good conscience ignore authorial intent here. As a responsible practitioner of BDSM, it disgusts me to listen to music about BDSM, written by someone who ignored safe play protocols and took advantage of the trust of the women who trusted him to rape and abuse them. Worse, he used a lot of sound sampling, including in several songs, samples of sexual moaning sounds. Turns out, at least one of his victims has come out to say that some of those samples were of her, and were recorded without her knowledge or permission. So I can\u2019t listen to any of his songs that feature moaning sounds without the knowledge that those sounds are an invasion of some woman\u2019s privacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:36:28-08:00","id":1287224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287075#post1287075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,,,unless the work in question is directly reflective of the author's views.</div> </div> </div> </div>What human creative work in all of history can't be argued to be directly reflective of the author's view?<br /> <br /> What human author is so coldly logical that their biases, views, and agendas are never present in their work? Esp. given that human creativity is completely anathema to &quot;Vulcan&quot; style thinking.<br /> <br /> As thoroughly gone over by Wil, this isn't about censorship or whatever political fantasies you want to have when people talk about this stuff.<br /> <br /> What this is about, is putting the Avery character in the VtM Prelude interactive fiction game the context of Zak S being responsible for her. She is not a harmless character. She's the product of a malicious asshole and when you play the game, you're supposed to get draw into Zak's hatred of others. It's about knowing that Zak is an expert at manipulating minority people into being shields for him (exactly what happened with Sarah when she came to his defenses about this... just like has been established is a consistent pattern for him) to deflect criticism of his work as being an attack on people he doesn't like.<br /> <br /> And people deserve to know about that before playing the game, or about how disgusting Woody Allen is and how that reflects on a lot of really iffy things in his movies, before buying/watching/etc. those products. Not have that knowledge hidden from them under some literary concept that the creative's biases don't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:52:13-08:00","id":1287234,"title":"","content":"I've already spoken my peace on the subject and I want it to be made clear that I do NOT defend Zak or his horrifying actions and that yes, people should be aware that Zak is a scumbag<br /> <br /> I'm gonna quietly withdraw from this thread and instead work on my Grand Theft Auto fan projects, it will be less stress and less drama for me and anyone else involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T13:54:50-08:00","id":1287236,"title":"","content":"Avery is the most awesome and sympathetic character in the game. She's basically the protagonist's older sister. I like her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:14:46-08:00","id":1287242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287236#post1287236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avery is the most awesome and sympathetic character in the game. She's basically the protagonist's older sister. I like her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never played the game, so I don't know what the deal is with Avery and what Zak had to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T14:56:12-08:00","id":1287269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287075#post1287075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DR I am opposed to real-life abuse, but censoring fiction like we live under totalitarian rule is not going to solve anything. If you don't like Zak Smith as a person and find his games problematic, then do what I do and simply don't buy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not erase Smith from history, even if I had the power to do so. I'm not O'Brian and this isn't 1984. At the very least erasing him would mean we could not learn bitter lessons from what he did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T15:08:00-08:00","id":1287281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287224#post1287224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What human creative work in all of history can't be argued to be directly reflective of the author's view?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - the artifacts are the products of people. The artifacts cannot and should be be separated from the people that made them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287224#post1287224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And people deserve to know about that before playing the game, or about how disgusting Woody Allen is and how that reflects on a lot of really iffy things in his movies, before buying/watching/etc. those products. Not have that knowledge hidden from them under some literary concept that the creative's biases don't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they should know these things. They should understand that the best bits of Allen, Cosby, and Smith are all still the products of sex offenders. Appreciating the works should come through that lens, of understanding the nature of the creatures that produced the artifact. There should be no room for &quot;the person is bad but the artifact is good&quot; thinking if it allows the artifact to stand on its own. The artifact should not stand on its own.<br /> <br /> The artifacts cannot and should be be separated from the people that made them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:03:27-08:00","id":1287315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith#post1287057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosby's... TV shows were funny \u2013 they were mostly good at what they were supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cosby Show, \u200bSeason 1 - Cliff Huxtable reveals that his reason for going to college at Hillman was because of Claire's interest in Hillman.<br /> <br /> Season 3 - Cliff celebrates his fiftieth birthday.<br /> <br /> Season 5 - Claire turns 46, establishing Cliff as <i>six years</i> her senior.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bClaire even mentions in an episode that she didn't get to go to her high school prom because Cliff had his finals that week.<br /> <br /> Meaning that an eighteen-year-old Cliff was romantically interested enough in a <i>twelve-year-old</i> Claire to have it shape his academic future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-12-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T17:46:23-08:00","id":1287358,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much of that was deliberate, and how much of it was the writers not worrying about how the details added up? I'm not defending Cosby, but he is guilty of only his own sins, so to speak, and not those of a rotating set of writers who did not think the math through.<br /> <br /> In any case, back on topic, the Cosby Show should always be viewed, first and foremost, as a TV series starring a sexual predator. The same is true of the RPG work of Smith - its quality doesn't matter, that Smith is a sexual predator, and abuser, matters. We should not let people off the hook who defend the books (or movies or TV shows) even if they do not defend the men. We should not be quick to forgive people who now apologize for something they had been told about, but refused to acknowledge, for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T18:14:02-08:00","id":1287367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287358#post1287358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, back on topic, the Cosby Show should always be viewed, first and foremost, as a TV series starring a sexual predator. The same is true of the RPG work of Smith - its quality doesn't matter, that Smith is a sexual predator, and abuser, matters. We should not let people off the hook who defend the books (or movies or TV shows) even if they do not defend the men. We should not be quick to forgive people who now apologize for something they had been told about, but refused to acknowledge, for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Jesus. Wasn't Charlaquin just saying upthread that &quot;don't buy his products&quot; was the only thing being advocated here? Going <i>pretty fucking far</i> beyond that, aren't you?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I have no idea who wrote most of the books in my RPG library. It's not something I care about, because it doesn't change the purpose I have in mind for them. I'm in the market for RPG books, I'm not looking to buy a sociopolitical lifestyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T19:09:17-08:00","id":1287386,"title":"","content":"(shrugs) That doesn't worry me.<br /> <br /> Some of the people who worked with Smith in the past are trying to own the problem and to do better, such as Ken Hite and Drive Thru RPG. Others who enabled Smith for years are not stepping up in that manner, or are trying to make the situation about them and their feelings, such as Mark Diaz Truman (and Magpie Games) and James Edward Raggi (of LotFP). Why should we ignore or dismiss the behavior of people like Truman or Raggi?<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm not calling for book burning or inflicting personal harm. But we can stop watching the movies of Allen, stop watching the Cosby Show, and stop buying, reading or using material from Smith. We can also stop buying, reading, or using the material from Truman and Raggi. There has to be a price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 02-12-2019, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T20:27:38-08:00","id":1287405,"title":"","content":"It sure worries me.<br /> <br /> Look, if you want to keep an enemies list of everyone who's been adjacent to this writer or failed to say harsh enough things about him, that's your prerogative. Don't dress it up in these lofty literary terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T21:54:06-08:00","id":1287420,"title":"","content":"I think we're missing a point here, though.<br /> Lewis Carrol and Micheal Jackson were known (allegied) pedophiles, Picasso was an abusive father and a chauvinist that said some of the worst things I ever read about women, Umberto Eco was an arrogant sack of shit, Walt Disney was a fascist and an abusive employer.<br /> <br /> But should we really say &quot;don't go see Guernica because Pigasso painted it&quot;? Had people thrown him away, refused to host showrooms or buy his paintings because of his behaviour, would this world be any better? Maybe we'd have condemned him to a mundane underpaid job, but at the same time we'd have lost his best works - perhaps he would have stopped after his Blue period and become a forgotten author.<br /> And some times it may not even matter. Whether or not Carrol was a pedophile, &quot;Alice in the Wonderland&quot; has no trace of it. Would there be any point in discarding the book?<br /> <br /> Now, Zak Smith is no Picasso, no Carrol. The world is probably going to go on just fine even without his contributions to the RPGs.<br /> We could lose some good supplements, though. As loathsome as he might be he's still a good author - or rather, exactly <i>because </i>he's a loathsome person he can be a good author, since a manipulative 300 years old vampire just comes out better when it's created by a manipulative sex addict with low morality. Honestly, I believe that Smith is perfect for the LotFP game line and he wouldn't be if he were a different kind of man.<br /> <br /> In the end, people make their own choices and if you don't want to contribute to something because you despise who's behind it then fine, God knows I've done that in the past too. But as it's wrong to keep the work apart from the author is also wrong to judge the work as if it was the author; yes, the author is going to be embedded there, somehow, but it doesn't have to be the part of him that you despise and it does not need to compromise the overall quality of the work itself.<br /> <br /> Sexual abusers should be put on trial and sentenced, but as a gamer I see no issue with them writing game supplements from behind bars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 02-13-2019, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T22:20:26-08:00","id":1287430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287405#post1287405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sure worries me.<br /> <br /> Look, if you want to keep an enemies list of everyone who's been adjacent to this writer or failed to say harsh enough things about him, that's your prerogative. Don't dress it up in these lofty literary terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, holding people who were aware of his other abusive conduct accountable for that and dismissed the allegations in order to continue working with him seems perfectly reasonable to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T06:48:28-08:00","id":1287518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287430#post1287430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, holding people who were aware of his other abusive conduct accountable for that and dismissed the allegations in order to continue working with him seems perfectly reasonable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think it\u2019s that simple. People like Zak S are good at manipulating people. In his case he got some of the very people he was abusing go forth and defend him vigorously. People saw how stridently they defended him and believed them, and defended him in turn. This in turn led to him having a large group of trusted voices defending him... and it snowballs, until there\u2019s enough doubt in peoples\u2019 minds.<br /> <br /> So I can\u2019t blame people for defending him in the past. But that no longer flies. No one has that excuse any more.<br /> <br /> As for the question of his work: let it burn. We lose nothing of value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T07:47:38-08:00","id":1287535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287518#post1287518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s that simple. People like Zak S are good at manipulating people. In his case he got some of the very people he was abusing go forth and defend him vigorously. People saw how stridently they defended him and believed them, and defended him in turn. This in turn led to him having a large group of trusted voices defending him... and it snowballs, until there\u2019s enough doubt in peoples\u2019 minds.<br /> <br /> So I can\u2019t blame people for defending him in the past. But that no longer flies. No one has that excuse any more.<br /> <br /> As for the question of his work: let it burn. We lose nothing of value.</div> </div> </div> </div>(sigh) I knew I should not have checked my forum notifications today....<br /> <br /> I hate Zak Smith too, but all I ask is that we simply don't buy his work because he is a shitty excuse for a person. Even Charlaquin herself said this is the best approach, she refuses to support him and so do I.<br /> <br /> I won't support Zak and I'm not buying his work, but I don't want to ban the works either.<br /> <br /> You know who else burned books and banned or de-platformed media that they deemed &quot;problematic&quot;?<br /> <br /> Hitler, Mussolini, Lenin, Stalin, Mao, Franco, the Kim Dynasty, and countless other totalitarian rulers, and every one of them were convinced they were justified in doing so.<br /> <br /> The road to Hell is paved with good intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 02-13-2019, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:05:36-08:00","id":1287538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287518#post1287518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s that simple. People like Zak S are good at manipulating people. In his case he got some of the very people he was abusing go forth and defend him vigorously. People saw how stridently they defended him and believed them, and defended him in turn. This in turn led to him having a large group of trusted voices defending him... and it snowballs, until there\u2019s enough doubt in peoples\u2019 minds.<br /> <br /> So I can\u2019t blame people for defending him in the past. But that no longer flies. No one has that excuse any more.<br /> <br /> As for the question of his work: let it burn. We lose nothing of value.</div> </div> </div> </div>People like Mike Mearls, who were made aware of his abusive conduct and then passed on the names and email addresses of the people who raised allegations against him to him, do not deserve our sympathy for being misled. They actively assisted harassment and abuse of others, and I both can and <i>will</i> blame people for that conduct. It's one thing to have gone 'well, I don't know, it's contested' - it's another to have gone 'I dunno' in the face of a hell of a lot of evidence, and it's another still to have gone 'i dunno, and also mate here are people who think you're an abusive lunatic and their names, which I know because they came to me to try and show me evidence of your conduct (which I have personally seen as a member of the social groups where the orchestrated harassment campaigns were organized)'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:28:17-08:00","id":1287564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287535#post1287535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (sigh) I knew I should not have checked my forum notifications today....<br /> <br /> I hate Zak Smith too, but all I ask is that we simply don't buy his work because he is a shitty excuse for a person. Even Charlaquin herself said this is the best approach, she refuses to support him and so do I.<br /> <br /> I won't support Zak and I'm not buying his work, but I don't want to ban the works either.<br /> <br /> You know who else burned books and banned or de-platformed media that they deemed &amp;quot;problematic&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> Hitler, Mussolini, Lenin, Stalin, Mao, Franco, the Kim Dynasty, and countless other totalitarian rulers, and every one of them were convinced they were justified in doing so.<br /> <br /> The road to Hell is paved with good intentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nonsense. First, I\u2019m not calling for his work to be banned. But even if his work was banned, nothing of value would be lost. <br /> <br /> Nobody should buy his work. Nobody should sell his work. Nobody should collaborate with him on future projects. And those that do will be judged appropriately. That isn\u2019t banning his work. It isn\u2019t censorship. It\u2019s a moral judgement. I don\u2019t support the work of rapists or those that enable them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:49:39-08:00","id":1287571,"title":"","content":"Why do I even fucking bother anymore? Like I said, I knew I should not have checked my forum notifications, because I'd get dragged back into this horrible nightmare.<br /> <br /> I hate Zak, but throwing a fit about his games (which are unrelated to his atrocious deeds) won't undo the crimes he committed. All we can do is simply not buy his works, which is what I'll do and what I have been doing even before this new information came to light.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm going to try and take a break from this forum for a few days. If any of you need me, you can contact me at either GTA Forums or RPG Pub</b><br /> <br /> <br /> GTA Forums (My username there is Big Fat Paulie)<br /> <a href=\"https://gtaforums.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://gtaforums.com/</a><br /> <br /> RPG Pub (My username there is Doc Sammy)<br /> <a href=\"https://rpgpub.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://rpgpub.com/</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T11:14:15-08:00","id":1287591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287564#post1287564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody should buy his work. Nobody should sell his work. Nobody should collaborate with him on future projects. And those that do will be judged appropriately. That isn\u2019t banning his work. It isn\u2019t censorship. It\u2019s a moral judgement. I don\u2019t support the work of rapists or those that enable them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This forever. And if I could stamp everything by Michael Jackson and Lewis Carrol as &quot;made by a pedophile&quot; I would. Let people know the nature of these creatures.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Fixed some wording. 02-13-2019, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T11:54:16-08:00","id":1287613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287591#post1287591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. This forever. And if you stamp everything by Michael Jackson and Lewis Carrol as &quot;made by a pedophile&quot; I would. Let people know the nature of these creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really not inspiring much confidence with your choice of examples, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 02-13-2019, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:03:31-08:00","id":1287618,"title":"","content":"The Death of the Author is about how you shouldn't interpret the text with the author in mind. Which is problematic in itself. I used to like The Mists of Avalon but it came out that Marion Zimmer Bradley covered for her pedo husband. She's dead and won't receive any royalties if I continue to buy the series, but I can't help but read into the young ages of many of the characters in sexual relationships. Not that I think that of any author who does that, but now that I know that about her it is a reminder every time it comes up in her books.<br /> <br /> That said, the reason Zak S was able to find so many victims was because so many who hired him refused to give credence to his victims. The art he created was a ticket to his sadism. He was enabled, and it is hard to divorce his art as a product from his actions when his art was a means to an end. Shit like this happens everywhere and it needs to stop. I once had a friend who turned out to be a serial rapist who targeted teenagers in the punk scene. When this all came out, so many in the punk community were like &quot;oh yeah I always knew he was a creep.&quot; I asked then why they helped him put on all ages shows if at best they knew he was inappropriate with teenagers, never got an answer. And it's hard to continue to participate in such communities when I'm pretty sure if something were to happen to me, no one would have my back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24887-sybil","name":"Sybil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:05:54-08:00","id":1287619,"title":"","content":"But what about the transient nature of the problem, or those creators that are long dead, or whose lives we know nothing about. I know that H.P. Lovecraft is well regarded in the RPG community, enough that Scion 2nd edition is going to have a supplement dedicated to his work. But I have never read his work nor do I wish to considering that my identity would probably be described as the scum of the Earth.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can't directly fault him, since I can't speak to the guy because he's dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:39:37-08:00","id":1287633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287591#post1287591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. This forever. And if you stamp everything by Michael Jackson and Lewis Carrol as &quot;made by a pedophile&quot; I would. Let people know the nature of these creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with you, but like Ostarion says, when it comes to individuals who are dead, I don't have an issue with people buying or enjoying the works of those people, since it's not like the person in question is getting any kind of benefit or support from people purchasing their work. They're dead and after they're dead I believe that there is more room to separate the creator from his creation. <br /> <br /> Ostarion mentioned HP Lovecraft who was an amazing writer and had a profound impact on pop culture. References to his works pop up constantly, in stories ,TV shows, video games and RPG books. At the same time, the man was horrifically racist to the point that there are places in some of his stories where his disgusting opinions leaked out onto the page and as a result, I simply won't touch those stories. But I also don't feel particularly bad about owning a compilation of his work, and enjoying some of his stories because the guy's dead and my purchasing and reading his work is not in any way supporting his disgusting views on race.<br /> <br /> Also, while it's very easy to demonstrate that HP Lovecraft was horrifically racist, at least with Michael Jackson and Lewis Carroll I don't believe it's ever been sufficiently demonstrated to prove that either of them were actually pedophiles who assaulted children, so I would be hesitant to permanently attach that label to them and their work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T13:01:44-08:00","id":1287641,"title":"","content":"I don't think this guys work is really a concern. He's a niche aspect of a niche industry. He's lauded for two supplements of an off-brand game, that have somehow managed to sell more copies than the core of the same game. His contributions to other games are little more than playtesting. He was a consultant for Vampire 5th edition, and while he's listed as a consultant for D&amp;D 5, they said he was just a playtester. By all means, refuse to review it. If you're a marketplace, refuse to sell his work (that is your right), and ignore the haters.<br /> <br /> Because his work isn't the issue with him, that's just how he gets his foot in the door. The issue with him and the rpg industry and fandom as a whole is the fact that he's one of those people we see all the time lately who manages to manipulate his way into some circle or another by manipulating perceptions around him and taking advantage of people who feel disillusioned. Reading the post by the ex-wife he abused and assaulted, I knew that there would be some people who would dismiss it as 'false rape accusations,' just like there would be people who maybe went through a bitter divorce and would blame it on that, or who simply wouldn't believe it all because 'why wouldn't you call the police.' Because people like that exist, and he's going to be a beacon to them, and just like he's done before, he's going to have them harass and threaten people on his behalf while he does the same. Just like when people call him out for his crap, he cries censorship, complains that anyone who has a problem with him is a prude, is against freedom of expression, and if you're pro freedom of expression, you should be defending him.<br /> <br /> Because that's what these people do. That's why a guy whose sole contribution to the contents of this board is consulting on one book of a shared IP, and who has made a video game (but not the one people like) is talked about here as if he's a pivotal figure, and not just another manipulative criminal using someone elses soapbox to self-aggrandize.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, comparing him to Woody Allen, Bill Cosby, Lovecraft or Lewis Carrol? Really? This guy's not even a footnote. Do you think a supplement for Lamentations of the Flame Princess is comparable to the frontier work of the Cosby Show, or as groundbreaking as the Cthulhu Mythos, do you think Disney's going to buy up his IP and make an animated movie because it's going to be a memorable story for later generations? Get real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287571#post1287571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do I even fucking bother anymore? Like I said, I knew I should not have checked my forum notifications, because I'd get dragged back into this horrible nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you have strong political views, but you seem to get frustrated because not everyone agrees with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T13:22:28-08:00","id":1287648,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I believe each piece of creative work should be evaluated on its own merits, regardless of who created it or why. This is especially important for projects involving many people, each of which influenced the final product in their own way. </span></span></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Then, separately from that, each creator should be judged on their actions and the consequences of those actions, regardless of their stated intentions. This includes whatever processes they used to create their work. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In any situation - I cannot condone starving a person to death (the logical outcome of denying a person all forms of support forever) because of their misdeeds. If someone is really abhorrent enough that they need to die in order to protect everyone around them, there are quicker and more merciful ways to kill.<br /> <br /> My reasoning is that if we discard everything ever made by anyone who did something we find abhorrent, an indeterminate-but-probably-very-large fraction of human culture will be cast aside, including much that people today find helpful, beautiful, and uplifting. Moreover, if we carry that principle of zero-tolerance forward, our evolving standards for morality will gradually erode more of our past and present culture.<br /> <br /> Besides that, I lack confidence that boycotting a creator's work will change them, not least because not all creators live off of royalties. It feels like a very passive-aggressive kind of punishment, undertaken to reassure the boycotter of their own morality rather than actually making a measurable positive change for anyone. Some more proactive options include:<br /> <br /> * Staging protests, attempt to get the creator fired or banned from a venue<br /> * Start or contribute to a support program for the creator's victims<br /> * Publish competing work - especially work that riffs on the original in a way that highlights the creator's failings. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-13-2019, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:14:15-08:00","id":1287694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287641#post1287641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, comparing him to Woody Allen, Bill Cosby, Lovecraft or Lewis Carrol? Really?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a statement to make a rhetorical point - it doesn't matter how good the artifact is if the artist is a shitbag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:06:20-08:00","id":1287725,"title":"","content":"I'll chime in to affirm that death of the author is an interpretive perspective about how the meaning of a work isn't dependant on the author's intention, not so much that a reader's view of an author's personality doesn't colour their interpretation of a work, and certainly not that you are obliged to disregard it when making purchases. One can absolutely boycott an author and still employ an analytical approach based on the death of the author.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:37:54-08:00","id":1287775,"title":"","content":"Just a few thoughts<br /> <br /> There are tons of &quot;Thing Producer&quot;s out there. (TP)<br /> <br /> If we stop supporting TP 100 and buy from TP 90, are we really hurting ourselves?<br /> <br /> If I'm TP 90, and not quite as good as TP 100, well, I'm still gonna do my best, but if people don't give a crap about what a bad person TP 100 is, what's the point of me trying to be a good person? I might as well just kick all the puppies I want cause it really doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Tho actually, I think character matters.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'll buy any more of TP 100's stuff, prolly won't watch it either cause for me, on a personal level, it loses a lot of it's appeal. If I already own some of TP 100's stuff. Well, honestly, I may or may not get rid of it, but if I do keep it, I may not bring myself to use it, dunno<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I think my reaction is gonna vary based on what TP 100 did and how much I like TP 100's product, but you can be sure I'll have a lower opinion of TP 100 himself. Not that that may mean a lot, but I still think character matters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T23:24:01-08:00","id":1287870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287564#post1287564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody should buy his work. Nobody should sell his work. Nobody should collaborate with him on future projects. And those that do will be judged appropriately. That isn\u2019t banning his work. It isn\u2019t censorship.</div> </div> </div> </div>The equivalent terms in current English are&quot;bigotry&quot; or &quot;fanaticism&quot;.<br /> Can you say &quot;kill them all, for the Lord will recognize his own&quot; for me? :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the same time, the man was horrifically racist to the point that there are places in some of his stories where his disgusting opinions leaked out onto the page and as a result, </div> </div> </div>The first thing they taught me in high school history classes was that you can't judge the past with the eyes of the modern world - ethnocentrism works even when we look to different times, not simply to different modern-day cultures. We all know nowadays that there are no scientific bases advocating for white supremacy, yet the situation was quite different a hundred years ago. Physiognomy and phrenology were really popular up to the beginning of the 20th century and we had several scientists (Gall, Lombroso, Hollander) publishing books on how black people were inherenlty more aggressive and bestial.<br /> And these doctors published those papers in good faith, looking for experimental data that were actually there- they simply misinterpreted their meaning (i.e.,of course black people have a predisposition to crime if you make them grow up with no rights in poverty).<br /> <br /> These pseudosciences were picked up by several literary artists of the period, like Dickens or Wilde, which talked about them in their books and made their characters use them to profile their villains. In the 19th century was even common for employers to ask their prospected employees for a character reference from a phrenologist that certified their predisposition to honesty.<br /> So, I can't really criticize Lovecraft for believing in white supremacy when half of the scientific world published papers in its favour and I believe it's insane to hold such a thing against him now, judging him from our 21th century perspective. Our grandfathers (literally them) were racists, the heroes of WW1 were horribly misogynists and the more we go back in time the worse it gets.<br /> <br /> The problem is that we <i>still have</i> white supremacists and pseudoscientists even with every data pointing us to the opposite direction, not that a hundred years ago it was a believable position for a rational man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 02-14-2019, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T23:41:09-08:00","id":1287874,"title":"","content":"Refusing to financially support abusers is not bigotry or fanaticism, nor is judging people by the company they keep. Perhaps the word you were looking for is 'discrimination'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T23:55:05-08:00","id":1287879,"title":"","content":"Lovecraft did a lot more than \u201cbelieve in scientific racism\u201d (which by the way, is still racism, and it is naieve to assume that the scientists who propped those ideas up were acting in good faith. Those scientists were not innocently misinterpreting data, they were doing bad science - starting from an assumption that supported their preexisting worldviews and looking for evidence to support those biased assumptions). He expressed some truly racist views that had next to nothing to do with the (racist) scientific thinking of the time. It\u2019s also trying to give him his cake and feed it to him too to say that he was just going along with the science of his time, considering the fact that THE central theme uniting his horror stories was the idea that it was hubris to think science gives us any true understanding of the universe.<br /> <br /> Should we take the historical context in which a work was created into account? Absolutely! It\u2019s very important when talking about, for example, Loveraft\u2019s racism to note that he wasn\u2019t some isolated crackpot, a lot of people at the time thought exactly the way he did, including the scientific community. It\u2019s also worth noting that the scientific community was (and still largely is) dominated by affluent white men, most of them on the older side. It\u2019s also important not to assume that because affluent white men were generally in agreement about certain things that \u201ceveryone thought that way.\u201d It is important to note that there were different social norms at the time, and equally important not to note who did and did not have a say in what was socially acceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-14-2019, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T06:08:35-08:00","id":1287915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287874#post1287874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Refusing to financially support abusers is not bigotry or fanaticism, nor is judging people by the company they keep. Perhaps the word you were looking for is 'discrimination'.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but what is the end goal here? To mildly inconvenience the abusers by reducing their profit margin? To reform them? To shut them out of human society forever? To kill them in a deniable fashion by distributing responsibility among a large number of people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T06:46:01-08:00","id":1287922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287915#post1287915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, but what is the end goal here? To mildly inconvenience the abusers by reducing their profit margin? To reform them? To shut them out of human society forever? To kill them in a deniable fashion by distributing responsibility among a large number of people?</div> </div> </div> </div>To exert pressure on those who engage in unacceptable conduct (e.g, domestic abuse or serial harassment) in order to change the society we live in using the most effective fulcrum available in a capitalist society, which is money. Boycotts aren't exactly a new idea, my friend - they're a well founded, exhaustively practiced piece of praxis. It is, quite literally, putting your money where your mouth is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:58:33-08:00","id":1287961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287915#post1287915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, but what is the end goal here? To mildly inconvenience the abusers by reducing their profit margin? To reform them? To shut them out of human society forever? To kill them in a deniable fashion by distributing responsibility among a large number of people?</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, denying them the prestige and support that they use as a shield and as leverage to abuse others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:14:23-08:00","id":1288003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287922#post1287922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To exert pressure on those who engage in unacceptable conduct (e.g, domestic abuse or serial harassment) in order to change the society we live in using the most effective fulcrum available in a capitalist society, which is money. Boycotts aren't exactly a new idea, my friend - they're a well founded, exhaustively practiced piece of praxis. It is, quite literally, putting your money where your mouth is.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The efficacy of boycotts depends on the target and how they are funded. A person is not necessarily a company, nor necessarily tied to a company in such a way that boycotting the company has a meaningful impact on the person. <br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is - a blanket refusal to buy any work connected to an abuser, without any further consideration for the context of the work, is an indiscriminate strategy. <br /> <br /> Besides that - you didn't really answer my question. What <i>exactly</i> is the change you're trying to create in society? Be as specific as possible. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>macd21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1287961#post1287961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, denying them the prestige and support that they use as a shield and as leverage to abuse others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes back to what I suggested before about staging protests. Boycotting can be a useful component of a protest, but just silently refusing to buy things has much less punch. It's the combination of refusing to buy things, AND the publicly announced conditional reason for not buying things, that motivates for-profit companies to fire people and change HR policy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T12:28:20-08:00","id":1288035,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that people have been pretty clear about what they want. My read of the situation is that most people want two things when they talk about deplatforming and not supporting abusers, in general: 1.) that they never find work again, and 2.) if they might find work, that companies know they risk not making money off that product.<br /> <br /> Like... It shouldn't be controversial to say &quot;no abusers or enablers of abuse in our space&quot;.<br /> <br /> To the point about protests/boycotts not necessarily being effective, that's likely not true in the tabletop industry. The profit margins on RPG products is stupid low. Very few people in TTRPGs are making bank on their products, so a protest can reach critical mass much more easily because many companies feel every lost sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:02:46-08:00","id":1288067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1288003#post1288003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The efficacy of boycotts depends on the target and how they are funded. A person is not necessarily a company, nor necessarily tied to a company in such a way that boycotting the company has a meaningful impact on the person. <br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is - a blanket refusal to buy any work connected to an abuser, without any further consideration for the context of the work, is an indiscriminate strategy. <br /> <br /> Besides that - you didn't really answer my question. What <i>exactly</i> is the change you're trying to create in society? Be as specific as possible. </span></span></span></div><br /> That goes back to what I suggested before about staging protests. Boycotting can be a useful component of a protest, but just silently refusing to buy things has much less punch. It's the combination of refusing to buy things, AND the publicly announced conditional reason for not buying things, that motivates for-profit companies to fire people and change HR policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Saedar said, that\u2019s not really true in the RPG industry, especially on the scale Zak S usually operates at. His career in the RPG industry is probably dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:43:49-08:00","id":1288106,"title":"","content":"Well, his career in the RPG industry is now pretty well tied to LotFP; which doesn't have the best history with all this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T17:45:13-08:00","id":1288123,"title":"","content":"Yes, Raggi and LotFP is probably the only ally or friend Smith has left. So they are his only option, aside from self publishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T19:54:16-08:00","id":1288150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1288003#post1288003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The efficacy of boycotts depends on the target and how they are funded. A person is not necessarily a company, nor necessarily tied to a company in such a way that boycotting the company has a meaningful impact on the person.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is - a blanket refusal to buy any work connected to an abuser, without any further consideration for the context of the work, is an indiscriminate strategy.<br /> <br /> Besides that - you didn't really answer my question. What <i>exactly</i> is the change you're trying to create in society? Be as specific as possible. </span></span></span></div><br /> That goes back to what I suggested before about staging protests. Boycotting can be a useful component of a protest, but just silently refusing to buy things has much less punch. It's the combination of refusing to buy things, AND the publicly announced conditional reason for not buying things, that motivates for-profit companies to fire people and change HR policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct that the efficacy of boycotts depends on the target and how they're funded, and that protests are also important. Good thing both are going on! Good thing tabletop gaming is a small enough industry that a few hundred lost sales are visible and a few thousand undeniably significant, especially in conjunction with extremely vocal protests. What we want is very clear: A tabletop community that does not shelter or abide abusers and serial harassers, and which does not employ those who victimize vulnerable people. There is no room for arguing this has not been argued ad nauseaum. Further, our boycott is anything but indiscriminate. It is both carefully considered and based on a concrete difference between companies and products that put money into the hands of abusers and those that don't. You suggest we aren't considering the 'context', but I submit the following: The context of these works is not great art, it's fuckin' elfgames for nerds of which a great many of high quality are available. We have weighed the value of the works against the value of our dollar and against the moral value (or lack of) involved in handing that dollar to abusers and those who support them and found that the scales are tipped against buying the works anyway. That is the context. It is not one we are ignoring - it is one we are actively involved in considering, shaping, and interpreting.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be blunt. Quit the mealy mouthed, hand-wringing bullshit about 'oh but what're you trying to achieve and think of the context!!' and come out and say what you really want to say. You don't think people should avoid buying products that put money directly into the hands of an abuser and those who enable him. At least be a big enough woman, man, enby or other to own your statements rather than trying to present it as anything else. I have no patience left for this whinging nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:42:40-08:00","id":1288190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1287057-barthes-is-wrong-allen-cosby-and-smith?p=1288106#post1288106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, his career in the RPG industry is now pretty well tied to LotFP; which doesn't have the best history with all this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>LotFP are going to have to decide which is more important: continuing to work with Zak, or selling material on drivethrurpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}